invariant: INV-26
file: handshake_post.c
catches: test/lint-quic-surface.sh
reason: handshake_post.c includes aes_traffic_key.h, the one header that
  gives the traffic key a body, so the file that rekeys a direction on a
  TLS KeyUpdate could declare an aes_traffic_key, fill it from a traffic
  secret and run it through a path nobody reviewed for a secret key.
  aes_traffic_key.h names the files admitted to it, and
  tools/quic-footprint.py reads that list, so lint-quic-surface fails on
  any other file that includes it.

--- old
#include "handshake_post.h"
--- new
#include "handshake_post.h"
#include "aes_traffic_key.h"
